  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION, OPERATIONS, AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Organization. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Permian Express Partners LLC ("PEP") is a joint venture, owned 87.7% by ET CC Holdings LLC ("ET CC"), a wholly owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP ("Energy Transfer"), and 12.3% by Mid-Point Pipeline LLC which is owned by ExxonMobil Pipeline Company. ET CC maintains a controlling financial and voting interest in PEP and is the operator of PEP. PEP owns a 40% membership interest in Bakken Holdings Company LLC and a 100% membership interest in Permian Express Partners Operating LLC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Operations. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;PEP is a Delaware limited liability company engaged in the transportation of crude oil.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Regulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;. PEP's crude oil transportation activities are subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") and various state authorities. Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as rates, underlying accounting practices, and rate-making agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Basis of Presentation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America ("GAAP"). The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) subsidiaries are reflected on the equity method whereas GAAP requires that all majority-owned subsidiaries be consolidated (2) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and the statement of cash flows and (3) use of FERC approved depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;These interim financial statements should be read in conjunction with the financial statements and notes thereto contained in the PEP FERC Form 6 for the year ended December 31, 2025. The financial statements are unaudited, but in the opinion of management, all adjustments have been made that are necessary to fairly state the financial position, results of operations and cash flows for the periods presented. Certain information and notes that would substantially duplicate the disclosures contained in the most recent FERC Form 6 have been omitted.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 12.0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;NOTE B - SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 12.0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Accrued capital expenditures as of June 30, 2026 and 2025 were $1.4 million and $1.8 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
